Subject: [overlay 0001] Export rerelease game entry points on macOS/Apple

The rerelease game module (subprojects/rerelease-game) marks its GetGameAPI /
GetCGameAPI entry points with Q2DLL_EXPORT, whose non-Windows branch only sets
visibility("default") for __linux__/__FreeBSD__/__OpenBSD__. macOS (__APPLE__)
falls through to an empty define, so under the build's -fvisibility=hidden the
entry points are hidden and the engine's Sys_GetProcAddress("GetGameAPI") returns
NULL -> "Failed to load game library". Add __APPLE__ to the visibility branch.

Upstream gap: the rerelease game submodule never targeted Apple platforms. The
same fix is needed for the iOS build (also __APPLE__).

Apply from the vendor root:  patch -p1 -d vendor/q2repro < this
--- a/subprojects/rerelease-game/rerelease/game.h
+++ b/subprojects/rerelease-game/rerelease/game.h
@@ -102,7 +102,7 @@ constexpr bit_t<n> bit_v = 1ull << n;

 #if defined(_WIN32)
     #define Q2DLL_EXPORT   __declspec( dllexport )
-#elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__OpenBSD__)
+#elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__OpenBSD__) || defined(__APPLE__)
     #define Q2DLL_EXPORT   __attribute__((visibility("default")))
 #else
     #define Q2DLL_EXPORT
